          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness reports a very quick observation of a very bright white ball appearing to come towards them and disappearing as it ascends into the sky. No particular noise was heard. No other testimony was collected. The description of the phenomenon suggests a reflection of the sun on an Iridium satellite (see http://www.cnes-geipan.fr/index.php?id=299).). The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of an Iridium flash.",
